<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/camera_registration_portal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/camera_registration_portal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Whether the subject's publisher operates a public opt-in camera-registration/integration portal — the vendor white-label `Connect <Place>` (Axon Fusus) surface shape (P36.76 / R11-ACQ-31). A programme-level existence fact about the published portal page — never registrant content: the portal exists as a public programme surface; what it registrant-carries is out of scope by construction (SIG-PUB-002; R11-A16 — programme facts, never registrant bytes). Distinct from `portal_exists` (a transparency portal) and from `deployment_exists` (a deployment's world existence)." .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/camera_registration_portal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0> .
