<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/configured_sharing_partner> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A configured sharing/access partner of the subject — one endpoint of a §12.2 configured_access edge (§29.3 reconciles the set; the subject's own snapshot or audit row asserts the edge). Written as an entity-ref claim under P31.6 / ADR-113 — the partner's portal identifier for portal-sourced edges (Eyes on Flock slugs), else a partner-organisation ref under ADR-112's identity rules (audit workbooks, the NVLS pooled-lookup vendor constant)." .
