<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/disclosure_field_state> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Per-field disclosure-completeness state for a mandated filing ('answered'/'present_but_empty'/'absent'). NOT ADJUDICATED: each claim's discriminating key is the mandated-field name, carried in raw_value, so a per-(subject, predicate) envelope would collapse distinct fields into one 'state' — a fabricated decision. Recorded but deliberately not adjudicated (§12.4, SIG-RECON-013); the claims stay visible on the subject." .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/disclosure_field_state> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0> .
