<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/enforcement_count> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The operator-published aggregate count of automated-enforcement outcomes (warnings/violations) for a camera or programme subject over a declared period — a claim carries its `period` and `measure` fields beside the integer value, keyed camera × month or site × quarter as published. Aggregate rows only: never a per-violation, plate, person, trip or citation record (P36.6 / R11-ACQ-10, I8 NEW-7) — the aggregate admission is distinct from the connector-forbidden `camera_count` device-count genre, and Part VIII prohibits the row-level surfaces this predicate deliberately replaces." .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/enforcement_count> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0> .
