<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_defect> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_defect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A recorded geometry-defect marking on a registry-observed subject: the defect class an ingest detector or the append-only correction pass found in the published coordinate pair — `axis_swap` (the pair sits outside the declared extent and the transposed pair sits inside it), `null_island` (the pair is at/near (0,0)), `sign_flip` (the pair sits outside the declared extent and negating exactly one axis lands it inside), or `wrong_jurisdiction` (the pair contradicts the declared extent and no transposition or sign flip rescues it). The observed pair, the declared extent it failed and the detector version ride the claim's evidence; the claim only MARKS the defect — the original coordinate claims stand and any corrected coordinate is a new `camera_latitude`/`camera_longitude` claim citing the originals in `derived_from_claim_ids` (P35.16 / R11-DATA-01, F-322, SIG-GEO-008, SIG-IDENT-004, SIG-ONTO-011)." .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_defect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0> .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_defect> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "geometry_defect"@en .
