<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_defect> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/objectKind> "literal" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_defect> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/resolutionStrategy> "never_resolve" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_defect> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/valueDatatype> "string" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_defect> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/volatilityClass> "IMMUTABLE" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_kind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_kind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The geometry shape kind a record declares for its subject — a `GeometryKind` member (area | line | point) of the ontology enum (§19, SIG-GEO-003). An automated-traffic-enforcement zone or a published camera programme area is an `area`, never a device point; an enforced route or corridor segment is a `line`. Registered by P36.3 (ACQ-03) so the closed vocabulary accepts the `geometry_kind=\"area\"` values P36.4's programme-area emit and P36.6's ATE zone layers assert." .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/geometry_kind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0> .
