<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_area> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/halfLife> "infinite" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_area> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/resolutionStrategy> "authoritative_source_wins" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_area> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/valueDatatype> "string" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_area> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/volatilityClass> "IMMUTABLE" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The operator-published aggregate count of programme outcomes — applications received, under review, approved, declined, rebates funded, cameras funded — for a programme-area subject over a declared period. A claim carries its `period` and `measure` fields beside the integer value, plus `series` naming the published measure column when one row fans out into per-status series. Aggregate rows only: never a per-registrant, name, address, location, plate, or device record (P36.7 / R11-ACQ-11) — distinct from `enforcement_count` (enforcement outcomes) and from the connector-forbidden `camera_count` device-count genre." .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0> .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "programme_count"@en .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/cardinality> "multi" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/halfLife> "6mo" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/objectKind> "literal" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/resolutionStrategy> "interval_union" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/valueDatatype> "integer" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/programme_count> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/volatilityClass> "VOLATILE" .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/published_by> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/published_by> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The publisher of the source dataset this subject's claims derive from — PUBLISHER provenance, never an operational role. P35.26 / SIG-TRUST-003: the publisher label is recorded as `published_by` (the generic sibling of `camera_registry_publisher` for non-registry sources — e.g. \"OpenStreetMap contributors\", \"EFF & MuckRock — Data Driven (2018)\"); it never evidences camera operation, ownership, vendor or access status, and — a provenance role — never mints an organisation entity-ref (ADR-112/ADR-122)." .
<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0/published_by> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/vocab/predicate/1.0.0> .
